# Local-bias comparison handoff

Read `REPORT.md` for the complete source-exposed analytic comparison. It supports the positive classical actual-member construction at the supplied premises, with the mandatory root qualification, and preserves finite failure routes and all physical supplier limits. It is not an audit or a root acceptance record.

The coefficient map is h_Ising=h_occupation/2+(1/4)sum J_occupation and J_Ising=-J_occupation/4. After collection, the occupation minimum flip gap is twice the Ising dominance margin. Positive physical block decompositions and their scalar/norm budgets must still be priced separately.

Publication wording should use a positive **inverse-temperature** lower bound (equivalently an upper temperature bound in a fixed convention). Both frozen proofs contain a prose “temperature lower bound” slip while their displayed beta conditions are correct. Leave those historical bytes exact and state the qualification explicitly. The O(L) switch summary additionally requires bounded reserves, k_0=O(L), and bounded profile factors; r>=1 is inherited, D_max denotes a logical routing span, and the rank obstruction applies to full-rank inputs.

Fixed local source-class tolerances do not imply fixed dynamic pulse/timing precision or full-output closeness to a prescribed nominal generator. The exact retained marginal is formed after the actual-member nominal quench and ideal compression; the faulty actual midpoint cannot silently replace it. All old aging, full-clock turn-on norms, scalar/channel/work accounts, endpoint guards, reference/garbage records and same-actual-baseline simulator premises remain required.

`SOURCE_MANIFEST.json` pins the two complete new source snapshots and references the existing immutable recovery packet for prior sources. All 31 independent freeze members were reverified unchanged. `EXPOSURE_AND_READ_COVERAGE.md` records the timing and shared-context limits. `metadata_runs/` contains the actual capture and validation child-process receipts. No scientific program was run, and no unrelated files, Git state, PR, audit state, checkpoint, lock, axiom or editable prompt changed.

`FINAL_FREEZE.json` is the final manifest for this one comparison deliverable. Its hash and the report hash are provided in the final handoff message. No optional boundary candidate or rotated-Gibbs source was read, and no external science review is implied by the metadata verifier.
